WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.500
Trace a ChEMBL measurement from its source assay and publication to a researcher-approved annotation.

00:00:06.500 --> 00:00:11.825
Build a new workspace snapshot straight from the ChEMBL API.

00:00:11.825 --> 00:00:15.893
Choose a human target, a measurement type and an observation limit.

00:00:15.893 --> 00:00:21.198
Collection is an operator action, so it needs a local reviewer token.

00:00:21.198 --> 00:00:25.360
Observations, then linked assays, compounds and publications are fetched and their source responses saved.

00:00:25.360 --> 00:00:29.106
The job records the ChEMBL release and the number of observations collected.

00:00:29.106 --> 00:00:38.013
Open the new snapshot as its own workspace for search and review.

00:00:38.013 --> 00:00:41.790
All five collected EGFR IC50 observations are searchable right away.

00:00:41.800 --> 00:00:48.441
The demo dataset holds 1,000 EGFR and ERBB2 measurements from ChEMBL 37, kept as recorded.

00:00:48.441 --> 00:00:53.545
Quality checks are findings, not confirmed errors. Source errors await independent review.

00:00:53.555 --> 00:01:03.100
126 proposals wait for a researcher decision. Nothing is approved automatically.

00:01:03.100 --> 00:01:07.756
Queries are parsed into target, measurement type and a concentration bound.

00:01:07.756 --> 00:01:17.250
Results are split into matches, undetermined and outside criteria. Undetermined rows never count as matches.

00:01:17.250 --> 00:01:23.333
ERBB2 Ki results keep the source inequality (&gt;) instead of an exact value.

00:01:23.333 --> 00:01:32.700
A vague bound such as “about 100 nM” is held for clarification instead of guessed.

00:01:32.700 --> 00:01:36.337
The demo runs on a copy of the database, never the original.

00:01:36.337 --> 00:01:38.400
GPT-6.2 Sol reads the source record of observation 28786562 and proposes a review note.

00:01:38.400 --> 00:01:41.862
One Responses API call with structured output. No automatic retry, no automatic approval.

00:01:41.862 --> 00:01:52.650
Type, relation, value and units are matched to the source; only a passing proposal is queued for review.

00:01:52.650 --> 00:01:58.150
Model, token usage and request/response hashes are kept as an audit record.

00:01:58.150 --> 00:02:04.750
Even the model’s copy of the measurement must keep the source inequality &lt; to pass.

00:02:04.750 --> 00:02:09.550
The model proposal joins the same queue as every other proposal, awaiting review.

00:02:09.550 --> 00:02:15.639
The proposed note and the verified source measurement sit side by side.

00:02:15.639 --> 00:02:23.100
The saved ChEMBL record, checked against its hash, shows Kd &lt; 0.5 nM.

00:02:23.100 --> 00:02:27.680
Anyone can inspect evidence; recording a decision needs a reviewer token.

00:02:27.680 --> 00:02:29.900
Every decision — approve, defer or reject — carries a written rationale.

00:02:29.900 --> 00:02:41.350
This missing-value flag needs the original paper first, so it is deferred.

00:02:41.350 --> 00:02:45.350
The model note matches the source, so it is approved. Approval and applying are separate steps.

00:02:45.350 --> 00:02:54.059
The model note matches the source, so it is approved. Approval and applying are separate steps.

00:02:54.059 --> 00:03:02.550
Only the approved change is written to a new curated version. The source value is untouched.

00:03:02.550 --> 00:03:15.600
Until the index is refreshed, search refuses to serve a version that differs from the latest approvals.

00:03:15.600 --> 00:03:20.600
Search and the Obsidian vault share this published version.

00:03:20.600 --> 00:03:25.400
In the new index, observation 28786562 is still found with its source bound Kd &lt; 0.5 nM.

00:03:25.400 --> 00:03:34.650
Evidence shows the measurement, the assay and the publication behind one row.

00:03:34.650 --> 00:03:41.976
The vault published with the same version opens in Obsidian.

00:03:41.976 --> 00:03:45.567
The note shows the source measurement Kd &lt; 0.5 nM with its inequality.

00:03:45.567 --> 00:03:49.137
The approved review note is recorded in the same published version.

00:03:49.137 --> 00:03:57.100
Follow the link from the observation to the EGFR target note (CHEMBL203).

00:03:57.100 --> 00:04:08.000
One observation links to its assay, compound, target, publication and research question.

00:04:08.000 --> 00:04:17.200
Drag and zoom through 2,008 notes and 5,000 links.

00:04:17.200 --> 00:04:22.700
Hovering the research question highlights its candidate links — candidates, not researcher judgements.

00:04:22.700 --> 00:04:26.050
Undoing a change never erases history; it opens a new rollback proposal.

00:04:26.050 --> 00:04:35.300
The rollback proposal is awaiting review. A reviewer must approve it before it can be applied.

00:04:35.300 --> 00:04:44.300
A built-in guide walks each role from collection to search, review and publishing.

00:04:44.300 --> 00:04:53.500
Collect data, check the source, review and publish the annotation, and propose a rollback for review.
